---
// Editorial policy — the single place for sourcing and evidence rules,
// so individual guides don't repeat the same disclaimers.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { STATUS_META } from '../data/confidence';
import { formatDate } from '../utils/dates';

const UPDATED = '2026-11-16';
const title = 'Editorial Policy — Plague Tale Legacy Guide';
const description =
  'How this unofficial Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy guide sources facts, labels player reports, dates snapshots, and handles corrections.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Editorial Policy', url: '/editorial/' },
];

const statuses = Object.values(STATUS_META);
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} pageType="article" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <article class="prose-page container max-w-3xl py-10">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-bone md:text-4xl">Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime={UPDATED}>{formatDate(UPDATED)}</time></p>

    <p>
      This page explains how every guide on {SITE.name} is researched and labelled. It applies to
      the whole site, so individual guides do not repeat it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where facts come from</h2>
    <p>Sources are used in this order of authority:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        The official <a href={SITE.steamUrl} rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Steam store page</a>
        (App {SITE.steamAppId}) and the game's Steam news hub: release date, price, platforms,
        system requirements, features, and patch notes.
      </li>
      <li>Official {SITE.developer} and {SITE.publisher} channels, including developer blogs and FAQs.</li>
      <li>Steam's global achievement statistics, quoted with the date they were read.</li>
      <li>Player reports from Steam reviews and discussions, and community walkthrough notes.</li>
      <li>The earlier A Plague Tale games, used only as clearly labelled series background.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>
      This site has not played or benchmarked the game itself. We do not present our own hands-on
      tests, invent menu paths, button prompts, frame rates, or routes, or turn a trailer shot into a
      confirmed mechanic. When a guide says "check this" or "load the save again", that is advice for
      you as the player, not a claim that we ran the test.
    </p>

    <h2>How player reports are labelled</h2>
    <p>
      When a specific claim comes from players rather than an official source, the sentence says so
      ("Steam reviewers report...", "walkthrough notes list..."). Pages built mainly on player reports
      carry the "Steam community reports" badge. Reports can be wrong, describe one platform, or change
      after a patch, so treat them as the best available information rather than a specification.
    </p>

    <h2>Confirmation badges</h2>
    <p>Every guide carries one of these labels at the top:</p>
    <ul>
      {
        statuses.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{s.icon} {s.label}</strong> — {s.description}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>Pages marked Unconfirmed are kept out of search indexes.</p>

    <h2>Dates and snapshots</h2>
    <p>
      Prices, review scores, and achievement unlock rates change daily. Wherever we quote one, we give
      the date it was read, and newer snapshots are added rather than silently overwriting older ones.
      The "Updated" date on a guide is the last time its content changed.
    </p>

    <h2>Patches</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.developer} has patched the game since its August 27, 2026 release, notably the October 6
      bug-fix update. Guides note which fixes apply, but a later patch can change behaviour before we
      update a page.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something is wrong or out of date, email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with the page URL and, ideally,
      a link or screenshot. Confirmed corrections are made to the page and its updated date is changed.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      This is an unofficial fan site, not affiliated with {SITE.developer} or {SITE.publisher}. The
      site may carry advertising; advertisers have no say in what we write. See the
      <a href="/about/">About page</a>, <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>, and
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
